Clean-room lexica for AR, DE, EN, ES, FR, HI, ID, IT, JA, KO, PT, RU, TR, VI, ZH
  This package no longer embeds HurtLex. HurtLex is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  (NonCommercial), and that term is why this project replaced it. The
  lexica below are original works assembled from license-clean sources.

  English Wiktionary and the native Wiktionaries (fr, ja, tr, ru, pt, it,
  ko, id, vi, zh, ar, de, hi)
    Source: https://en.wiktionary.org and the corresponding native wiki
    License: CC BY-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
    Share-alike: any redistribution of this data, or of a derivative
    lexicon built from it, must carry CC BY-SA 4.0 and attribution.

  LDNOOBW (List of Dirty, Naughty, Obscene, and Otherwise Bad Words)
    Source: https://github.com/LDNOOBW
    License: CC BY 4.0, attribution only

  washyourmouth
    License: MIT

  textdetox multilingual_toxic_lexicon
    Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/textdetox/multilingual_toxic_lexicon
    License: OpenRAIL++, a use-restricted license, not an OSI-approved one.
    Recorded as its own class rather than folded in with the CC sources
    above, since its terms differ from share-alike or attribution-only.

  Vietnamese candidate mining only, not redistributed
    zerostratos/vietnamese_toxic_core, Apache-2.0
    uitnlp/vihsd (UIT-ViHSD), MIT

  The NonCommercial term is gone from this package. Share-alike remains,
  carried by Wiktionary rather than HurtLex.

Language identification slices derived from ELDC
  Source: https://github.com/nitotm/eldc
  Revision: a0301db809ff2e48a418018aa5359fb0c4354eb8
  License: Apache-2.0
  The .detect files carry fifteen language profiles from the upstream model.

Sparse tables (*-sparse-v2.bin, es-chargram-v1.bin)
  Trained in this repository from the corpora recorded in
  resources/datasets/source-lock-v1.json. See that file for each source's license.

The sparse toxicity tables were trained on these corpora. The tables contain
hashed integer weights and no corpus text.

